# core.autocrlf=true on the Windows workstations rewrites checkouts to CRLF.
# For shell scripts that is not cosmetic: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang and
# `set -euo pipefail\r` fail outright on Linux, and these scripts are meant to
# run on the game host. CLAUDE.md already requires LF everywhere; this makes
# git enforce it instead of relying on every tool behaving.
*.sh text eol=lf
# The PATH shims under deploy/tests have no extension and are scripts all the
# same; without this line autocrlf checks them out CRLF and the syntax suite
# fails on a clean tree.
deploy/tests/shims/* text eol=lf
# The Fire page's woff2 faces are binary. Git's own detection already treats
# them so, but the whole point of this file is that a Windows checkout must not
# be allowed to rewrite bytes, and a font rewritten as text is a font that no
# longer loads. Saying it outright makes that independent of a heuristic.
*.woff2 binary
# OFL.txt is the upstream SIL Open Font License reproduced byte for byte,
# because the licence asks for its notice to travel with the fonts unaltered.
# One line of it ends in a space. That is upstream's text, not a defect to fix
# here, so the whitespace check must not read it as one.
web/games/fire/v2/fonts/OFL.txt -whitespace
# The launcher's modules and every tracked JSON document, for the same reason.
# `web/hosts.js` is imported by the pages and by `deploy/check-hosts.mjs`, the
# deploy gate runs `node` over both, and `web/games.json`, `web/mirrors.json`
# and `server.json` are parsed by python, by node and by the browser. None of
# those break on CR the way a shebang does, which is precisely why a CRLF
# checkout would go unnoticed here until a diff or a checksum disagreed with
# the published bytes. Every tracked file matching these patterns is LF in the
# index and in the worktree today, so this pins what is already true.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
